  entry .Error
    info
        - one fault in CSS text, with its line, column and reason
        + une faute dans du texte CSS, avec sa ligne, sa colonne et sa raison
    detail
        - Error 251: _invalid CSS at line `n` column `n`: `reason`_, with the reason's own
        - number as the subcode. One is raised for each problem found while reading a
        - stylesheet or parsing a selector, grammar or value; `read[Css]` collects them all
        - into a `Css.Errors`, while `SelectorList.parse` and `Css.Syntax.Matcher.check` raise a
        - single `Css.Error` through a `Tactic[Css.Error]`. Constructing one needs a
        - `Diagnostics`.
        + Erreur 251 : _invalid CSS at line `n` column `n`: `reason`_, avec le propre numéro de la
        + raison comme sous-code. Une erreur est levée pour chaque problème trouvé lors de la
        + lecture d'une feuille de style ou de l'analyse d'un sélecteur, d'une grammaire ou d'une
        + valeur ; `read[Css]` les rassemble toutes dans une `Css.Errors`, tandis que
        + `SelectorList.parse` et `Css.Syntax.Matcher.check` lèvent une seule `Css.Error` au moyen
        + d'une `Tactic[Css.Error]`. En construire une nécessite un `Diagnostics`.

        ```scala
        import soundness.*
        import strategies.throwUnsafely
        import errorDiagnostics.stackTracesDiagnostics

        capture[Css.Error](SelectorList.parse(t"a!")).reason
        // Css.Error.Reason.UnexpectedChar('!')
        ```
    refer cataclysm.Css.Errors
    entry .Reason
      info
          - why the CSS was invalid: the nine kinds of fault, each numbered
          + la raison pour laquelle le CSS était invalide : les neuf sortes de fautes, chacune
          + numérotée
      detail
          - A `Reason` is a `Clarification` with a `#number`, which becomes the error's subcode:
          + Une `Reason` est une `Clarification` dotée d'un `#number`, qui devient le sous-code de
          + l'erreur :

          ```tabular
          - column  Case
          - column  Code
          - column  Message
          - column  Note
          - row  `UnterminatedComment`  1  _a comment was not terminated_
          - row  `UnterminatedString`  2  _a string literal was not terminated_
          - row  `UnexpectedEnd`  3  _the input ended before a rule was closed_
          - row  `UnexpectedChar(char)`  4  _the character `char` was not expected here_
          - row  `EmptySelector`  5  _a selector was expected but none was found_  a rule with nothing before its `{`
          - row  `UnknownProperty(name)`  6  _`name` is not a recognized CSS property_
          - row  `BadValue(property, value)`  7  _`value` is not a valid value for the `property` property_
          - row  `UnsupportedValue(property, types)`  8  _the value of `property` uses an unsupported type_  the property's grammar uses value types the matcher does not implement, listed in `types`
          - row  `InvalidName(name)`  9  _`name` is not a valid CSS identifier_  a class or id
          + column  Cas
          + column  Code
          + column  Message
          + column  Remarque
          + row  `UnterminatedComment`  1  _a comment was not terminated_
          + row  `UnterminatedString`  2  _a string literal was not terminated_
          + row  `UnexpectedEnd`  3  _the input ended before a rule was closed_
          + row  `UnexpectedChar(char)`  4  _the character `char` was not expected here_
          + row  `EmptySelector`  5  _a selector was expected but none was found_  une règle sans rien avant son `{`
          + row  `UnknownProperty(name)`  6  _`name` is not a recognized CSS property_
          + row  `BadValue(property, value)`  7  _`value` is not a valid value for the `property` property_
          + row  `UnsupportedValue(property, types)`  8  _the value of `property` uses an unsupported type_  la grammaire de la propriété utilise des types de valeurs que le vérificateur n'implémente pas, listés dans `types`
          + row  `InvalidName(name)`  9  _`name` is not a valid CSS identifier_  une classe ou un identifiant
          ```
